# Claude — Run Instructions

## Access

- **URL**: <https://claude.ai>
- **Account**: use a benchmark-dedicated account (don't mix with personal/work conversations — context bleed risk)
- **Plan required**: **Claude Pro or Team** for Projects feature and full file-upload allowance. Free tier has tighter file-size limits and no Projects.
- **Model pin**: select the latest production Claude model in the dropdown at start of each session; record the exact ID in `runs/claude/session.md` (start + end). If model rev mid-session, restart and note it.

## Ingestion approach

For UC01 (and any Simple-mode UC with named files or URLs):

1. Create a **new Project** (left sidebar → "+ New project"). Name it: `Benchmark UC01 - DD financial`.
2. Add knowledge to the project:
   - Either upload the source files (preferred when files are available), or
   - Paste each source URL as a "Custom instructions" / URL reference. Note: Claude doesn't natively fetch arbitrary web URLs from Project knowledge — for UC01 specifically, upload the SEC EDGAR `.htm` files instead.
   - For UC01 the files are: `msft-fy24-10k.htm`, `msft-fy24-proxy.htm` (locally at `/tmp/uc01/`).
3. Verify both files appear in the Project knowledge panel.
4. Start a new conversation inside the Project.

For UC02 (Repeat mode): same as above; upload all per-source files into one Project.
For UC03 (Spreadsheet mode): paste the canonical template prompt; loop the obligation rows one per message (Claude doesn't have native row-by-row UI).

## Limits to know

- **Per-Project knowledge**: roughly 20 files / 30 MB each (Pro tier). Trim if a UC exceeds this.
- **Per-message attachments**: 5 files max in a single message (use Projects to bypass).
- **Format support**: PDF, DOCX, TXT, HTM/HTML, code files. Images supported but Claude historically weak on multi-tab Excel — flag for UC06.
- **Web URLs**: Claude does NOT fetch arbitrary URLs from message text by default. Use Projects + uploaded files instead.
- **Context window**: large but not infinite. UC04 (100+ contracts) and UC07 (M&A data room with 100+ files) will likely overflow — note in run report when this happens.

## Per-question protocol

1. Open the Project's main conversation.
2. Paste the question verbatim from `questions-only.md`. **No system prompt. No preamble.** Just the question text.
3. Wait for the full response.
4. Capture:
   - `prompt.txt` — verbatim what was typed
   - `answer.md` — Claude's full response, copy-pasted
   - `answer.pdf` — print-to-PDF of the conversation page (Cmd+P → Save as PDF)
   - `screenshot.png` — full-page screenshot
   - `notes.md` — any anomalies (refusals, partial responses, file-load errors, latency, citation patterns)
5. **Start a fresh conversation between questions** in the same Project. This prevents cross-question context bleed and matches Normain's per-insight isolation.

