## Known quirks to flag in grading

- Claude tends to be verbose. Penalize verbosity-without-substance (judge prompt should account for this).
- Strong on cited PDF passages; weaker on Excel multi-tab logic.
- Citation style differs from Normain's [1][2] inline marks — Claude uses prose references ("according to the 10-K's Item 1A...").
- Refuses (rare) usually around personal data or pay disclosures — unlikely to trigger on public SEC filings.

